exports[`additional tier-A render targets > codex matches its native golden tree 1`] = `
{
  ".codex/agents/wl-reviewer.toml": {
    "content": "name = "wl-reviewer"
description = "Observe the assigned fixture."
developer_instructions = "The conductor supplies wholeloopRoot from the packaged adapter root command. For every canonical wl command invoke Node with wholeloopRoot/bin/wl.mjs. Read shared protocols under wholeloopRoot/resources/protocols/. If the root or required evidence is absent, return a question; do not guess PATH or manufacture coverage.\\n\\nCanonical model tier: deep; inherit the current model unless the caller explicitly chooses an available model.\\nThis role cannot obtain a separate native sandbox from its custom-agent file. Use a read-only parent or the checked headless gate transport for repository inspection; a prompt alone does not enforce read-only access. Never repair source or report inaccessible evidence as observed.\\n\\n# Review\\n\\nReturn concrete evidence.\\n"

[features]
shell_tool = false
apps = false
plugins = false
memories = false
request_permissions_tool = false
",
    "mode": 420,
  },
  "bin/wl.mjs": {
    "content": "#!/usr/bin/env node
console.log("fixture core")
",
    "mode": 493,
  },
  "plugin.json": {
    "content": "{
  "$schema": "https://agent-plugins.org/schemas/1.0.0/plugin.schema.json",
  "name": "wholeloop",
  "version": "0.0.0",
  "description": "Define, build, roll out and learn through independent evidence-backed development steps.",
  "author": {
    "name": "Iván González Sáiz"
  },
  "license": "MIT",
  "homepage": "https://github.com/dreamingechoes/wholeloop",
  "repository": "https://github.com/dreamingechoes/wholeloop"
}
",
    "mode": 420,
  },
  "resources/protocols/core-invariants.md": {
    "content": "# Core invariants

Retain evidence.
",
    "mode": 420,
  },
  "skills/wl-next/SKILL.md": {
    "content": "---
name: wl-next
description: Continue fixture work.
---
Use the exact directory of this loaded SKILL.md reported by the client. If unavailable, ask for it. Its scripts/wl.mjs launcher imports the packaged core, even through an installed directory symlink. First call that launcher with adapter root --json and pass the returned root to delegated agents. Canonical wl commands below mean this launcher, never an unrelated executable on PATH.

# Next

Call wl next --json.
",
    "mode": 420,
  },
  "skills/wl-next/scripts/wl.mjs": {
    "content": "#!/usr/bin/env node
await import(new URL("../../../bin/wl.mjs", import.meta.url))
",
    "mode": 493,
  },
  "wholeloop-artifacts.json": {
